{#- AI art (owner decisions 2026-10-13, CLAUDE.md 4): the only way a page shows a ChatGPT illustration.
    `a` is a picture from pipeline/art.py (slots()/picture()); `lang` is the page's language ('ko', 'en', 'ja' …).
    The figure carries data-art and the <img> alt is the picture's alt in that language: it starts with '일러스트: ',
    'Illustration: ', 'イラスト：' …, so no one takes it for a photo. No caption: the owner dropped the on-image
    'AI 생성 이미지' label (2026-10-13 night, '다 빼'); /about/ says once that the illustrations are drawn with generative
    AI, and validate.py rejects that label on any page. It also rejects AI art anywhere else, on place pages, inside
    place cards and in structured data. A page gets only the pictures whose langs name its language (art.for_lang).
    decorative: the figure is hidden from screen readers (a band repeated on every list, the 404 gull, a small picture
    beside a heading) — the alt stays in the markup. Styles: templates/assets/css/49-art.css. -#}
{% macro figure(a, lang='ko', sizes='100vw', eager=false, cls='', decorative=false, high=false) -%}
<figure class="art{{ ' ' ~ cls if cls }}" data-art="{{ a.id }}"{% if decorative %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="{{ a.avif }}" sizes="{{ sizes }}"><source type="image/webp" srcset="{{ a.webp }}" sizes="{{ sizes }}"><img src="{{ a.src }}" alt="{{ a.alts[lang] }}" width="{{ a.w }}" height="{{ a.h }}" {% if high %}fetchpriority="high"{% elif not eager %}loading="lazy"{% endif %} decoding="async"></picture></figure>
{%- endmacro %}

{#- band(a): the header band of a page, above its H1 — the lists (D head-*), a theme page (H theme.head.<slug>), a
    video topic page (M videos.head.<topic>), a course page (I course.banner.<course id>) — a 2.4:1 strip, at most a
    fifth of a phone screen (css). In the first screen, so not lazy; not fetchpriority=high either, so on a slow phone it
    does not take the bandwidth the stylesheet and fonts need first (a 400w file at 1x). Nothing when the slot is empty. -#}
{% macro band(a, lang='ko') -%}
{% if a %}<div class="wrap art-band-wrap">{{ figure(a, lang, '(min-width: 1264px) 1200px, calc(100vw - 32px)', eager=true, cls='art-band', decorative=true) }}</div>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- banner(a, lang): a guide's campaign card (C·G camp-* in Korean, Q en-camp-* in English) at the top of its head —
    its printed words are the alt's; loaded like the band. -#}
{% macro banner(a, lang='ko') -%}
{% if a %}{{ figure(a, lang, '(min-width: 1000px) 440px, (min-width: 700px) 44vw, calc(100vw - 32px)', eager=true, cls='art-camp') }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- small(a): a small square picture on the 404 page and the empty search result (F art-*). -#}
{% macro small(a, lang='ko', hidden=false) -%}
{% if a %}<div class="art-small-wrap"{% if hidden %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ figure(a, lang, '200px', cls='art-small', decorative=true) }}</div>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- strip(a): a band at the head of a section further down a page (L area.<권역> on /map/, in the directory column):
    lazy, decorative. -#}
{% macro strip(a, lang='ko') -%}
{% if a %}{{ figure(a, lang, '(min-width: 1264px) 590px, (min-width: 1024px) 47vw, calc(100vw - 32px)', cls='art-band art-strip', decorative=true) }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- beside(a) — {% call artm.beside(a) %}<h3 …>…</h3>{% endcall %}: a small square picture beside a heading further down
    a page (J events.month.<MM> on /events/, N abroad.group.<group> on /abroad/): picture and heading in one row; lazy,
    decorative. Without a picture the heading alone, exactly as before. -#}
{% macro beside(a, lang='ko') -%}
{% if a %}<div class="art-hd">{{ figure(a, lang, '72px', cls='art-mark', decorative=true) }}{{ caller() }}</div>{% else %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- hero(a): the picture of a page head beside its title (S about.head): from 900px to the right of the title (the
    head's class has-art-hero), on phones below the lede; in the first screen — not lazy, no fetchpriority. The frame
    (520px from 900px, at most 560px, else the column) is a 4:3 cover of the 3:2 drawing (css 49-art), so the drawing
    is 1.125 times the frame's width: the sizes say that width. -#}
{% macro hero(a, lang='ko') -%}
{% if a %}{{ figure(a, lang, '(min-width: 900px) 585px, (min-width: 592px) 630px, calc((100vw - 32px) * 1.125)', eager=true, cls='art-hero') }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
